  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nHigh pressure is projected to retreat from the Middle-Ohio Valley \nand Central Appalachians as a cold front advances towards the area \ntoday. The front will then progress across the area late tonight and \nThursday as the parent low lumbers across James Bay and central \nQuebec. With little moisture accompanying the front, and a swift \nreturn of high pressure after its passage, benign weather is \ngenerally expected to persist through Saturday.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDuring the weekend, a tropical system is projected to invade the \nGulf States before merging with an upper trough. Precipitation \nchances will begin to increase across the forecast area as the \ntrough and low move into the Ohio Valley late Saturday night into \nSunday. Precipitation tapers off as the weakening system heads into \nthe Atlantic on Monday; however, this drier interlude is likely to \nbe short lived as another system passes to the north and ferries a \nfront across the area Tuesday into Wednesday.",
